## Refresh Ontology Designer map metadata without a full rebuild

Context: Saving an entity or relationship from the Ontology Designer always
rebuilt the whole map (`initOntologyMap()`), even for metadata-only edits
(label, emoji, direction, external-config badge). That reset layout and was
unnecessary when the graph topology did not change. Entity and relationship
saves now describe whether a rebuild is required; metadata-only updates patch
the existing D3 node or link in place, and create/rename/parent/endpoint
changes still rebuild.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-map.js
   Extract `_classHasExternalConfig` and `_appendMapExternalBadge`; add
   `refreshMapNodeFromConfig` and `refreshMapRelationshipFromConfig` to update
   label, icon, badge, and link direction/label on existing map elements;
   scope `refreshMapLinkDirection` to `ontologyMapSvg`.
2. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js
   Pass save callbacks `{ entityName|relationshipName, previousName,
   requiresMapRebuild }`; add `refreshMapAfterEntitySave` /
   `refreshMapAfterRelationshipSave` so map-tab saves incrementally refresh
   when topology is unchanged, otherwise rebuild; drop the redundant
   `refreshMapLinkDirection` call from relationship save.
3. tests/units/front/test_ontology_map_external_badge.py
   Point the `hasExternal` source contract at `_classHasExternalConfig`.
4. tests/units/front/test_ontology_map_incremental_refresh.py (new)
   Source-guard contracts for rebuild vs incremental refresh on entity and
   relationship saves, including scoped D3 selections.

